---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Counters"
  description="Compare counters that count up, count both ways, or use one shared order."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="Counters"
>
  <article class="counter-family">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structure family</p>
      <h1>Counters</h1>
      <p>
        A shared number gets tricky when several people change it at the same
        time. Some counters only go up, some also go down, and some use one
        shared order for every change.
      </p>
      <LessonIllustration id="structures-counters" />
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="g-counter-title">
      <header>
        <div>
          <p class="structure-kind">No shared order</p>
          <h2 id="g-counter-title">G-counter</h2>
          <p>A counter that can only go up.</p>
        </div>
        <code>g_counter_kernel</code>
      </header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Each person keeps their own count. When people share their counts,
            the counter keeps the highest number reported by each person and
            adds them together. A repeated or late message cannot add the same
            work twice.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Totals that never need to decrease</li>
            <li>Messages that may arrive late or more than once</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Updates</dt><dd>Increment only</dd></div>
          <div><dt>How copies combine</dt><dd>Keep each person's highest count</dd></div>
          <div><dt>What it remembers</dt><dd>One number per person</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/g-counter/">Read the G-counter lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="pn-counter-title">
      <header>
        <div>
          <p class="structure-kind">No shared order</p>
          <h2 id="pn-counter-title">PN-counter</h2>
          <p>A counter that can go up or down.</p>
        </div>
        <code>pn_counter_kernel</code>
      </header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            A PN-counter uses two G-counters. One records increases and the
            other records decreases. The visible total is the increases minus
            the decreases.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Offline counters that must increase and decrease</li>
            <li>Corrections that may arrive late or more than once</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Updates</dt><dd>Increment and decrement</dd></div>
          <div><dt>How copies combine</dt><dd>Combine both counters separately</dd></div>
          <div><dt>What it remembers</dt><dd>Two numbers per person</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/pn-counter/">Read the PN-counter lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="shared-counter-title">
      <header>
        <div>
          <p class="structure-kind">Uses shared order</p>
          <h2 id="shared-counter-title">SharedCounter</h2>
          <p>A counter that puts every change in one shared order.</p>
        </div>
        <code>counter_kernel</code>
      </header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Everyone sends their increases and decreases to one service. The
            service numbers each change and sends the same ordered list back
            to everyone. Each numbered change is used once.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Shared totals that already pass through one service</li>
            <li>Small summaries where everyone must use the same order</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Updates</dt><dd>Increase or decrease by a number</dd></div>
          <div><dt>How changes apply</dt><dd>Use each numbered change once</dd></div>
          <div><dt>What it remembers</dt><dd>The total and any changes still waiting</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/shared-counter/">Read the SharedCounter lesson</a>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through structures">
      <a href="/structures/">Browse all structure families</a>
      <a href="/structures/sets/">Continue to sets</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .counter-family {
    max-width: var(--measure-reading);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .page-intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }

  .page-intro > p:last-of-type {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .counter-family > section {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    background: var(--clear);
  }

  section > header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  section h2,
  section header p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-block: var(--space-1);
  }

  .structure-kind {
    color: var(--instrument);
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  section header code {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .structure-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(15rem, 0.7fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }

  .structure-body p,
  .structure-body h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .structure-body h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .structure-body ul {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
    border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  dl div {
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
  }

  dl div + div {
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line-faint);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  dd {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
  }

  .structure-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .structure-next {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  @media (width < 42rem) {
    .counter-family > section {
      padding: var(--space-4);
    }

    section > header,
    .structure-body {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    section > header {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
  }
</style>
